Absolutely. If your goal is to build a personal "game room" app that you can keep around and pull out whenever friends are together, I'd actually recommend building a collection of small games around one shared multiplayer system rather than building one huge game.

Here are some that would work particularly well:

🎮 Game ideas worth building
Game	Players	Why it's fun
Typing Wars	2–8	Race to type the same passage first
Quick Draw	2–10	See a prompt, draw it, everyone guesses
Word Blitz	2–12	Make words from random letters before time runs out
Trivia Battle	2–20	Everyone answers simultaneously
Guess the Person	3–12	Yes/no questions to identify a mystery person
Emoji Pictionary	2–12	Guess movies, songs, places, etc. from emojis
Categories	2–12	Given a category + letter, race to submit an answer
Higher or Lower	2–20	Predict whether the next number/card is higher or lower
