30. Success Criteria

The MVP is successful when:

A host can create a room.
Friends can join using a code.
Players appear in the lobby in real time.
The host can start a game.
All players receive synchronized game state.
Scores are calculated server-side.
Players can see live standings.
Players can play another game without creating another room.
The session produces a final winner.
A complete session can be played without requiring accounts.
31. Long-Term Vision

Party Arcade should eventually become a personal multiplayer game platform rather than a single game.

The long-term experience should be:

"We're bored. Open Party Arcade."

Choose a room → invite friends → pick a game → play → laugh → switch games → keep score → crown the champion.

The platform should make it possible to turn a random gathering into a competitive mini-game night in under two minutes.